---
layout: layouts/base.njk
pageKey: countries
title: "Country benchmark — Citere"
description: "The same documented false claims about Ukraine, asked in the local language, across the markets Russia targets. Repeat-rate per assistant and per market."
pagination:
  data: build.languages
  alias: lang
  size: 1
permalink: "{{ '/countries/' | loc(lang) }}"
---
{%- from "partials/bot-mark.njk" import botMark -%}
{%- set doc = copy.en.countries -%}
<nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="{{ '/' | url }}">Home</a> /
  {%- if navigation.has.benchmarks %} <a href="{{ '/benchmarks/' | url }}">Benchmarks</a> / {% endif %}
  <span aria-current="page">Countries</span></nav>
<div class="phead"><h1>{{ doc.data.h1 }}</h1>
  <p class="plead">{{ doc.data.lead | mdInline | safe }}</p></div>

<div class="grid4" style="margin-bottom:26px">
{%- for c in profiles.countries %}
  <a class="cc {{ c.key }}" href="{{ c.url | url }}"><div><div class="rank-n">#{{ loop.index }} by repeat-rate</div>
    <span class="flag">{{ c.key | flag }}</span>
    <h3>{{ c.name }}</h3><div class="stat">{{ c.repeatRate | rate }} repeat &middot; {{ c.n }} answers &middot; {{ c.language | languageName }}</div></div>
    <div class="bots-mini">{% for b in c.bots %}{{ botMark(logos, b, "sm") }}{% endfor %}</div></a>
{%- endfor %}
</div>

<div class="shead"><h2>{{ 'section.sameClaim' | t }}</h2><span style="font-size:13px;color:var(--dimmer)">all personas in each market's sample</span></div>
<div class="panel"><table>
  <caption class="visually-hidden">Repeat-rate per assistant in each market, with the spread between its best and worst</caption>
  <thead><tr><th scope="col">{{ 'col.chatbot' | t }}</th>
    {%- for c in profiles.countries %}<th scope="col">{{ c.key | flag }} {{ c.key | upper }}</th>{% endfor %}
    <th scope="col">{{ 'col.spread' | t }}</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {%- for row in profiles.matrix.rows %}
    <tr><td class="cl"><span class="markcell">{{ botMark(logos, row.chatbot, "sm", true) }}{{ row.name }}</span></td>
      {%- for cell in row.cells %}<td class="rmeta">{% if cell %}{{ cell.rate | rate }}{% else %}<span style="color:var(--dimmer)">&mdash;</span>{% endif %}</td>{% endfor %}
      <td class="rmeta" style="color:var({{ '--false' if row.spread > 0.025 else ('--mislead' if row.spread > 0.015 else '--dim') }})">{{ row.spread | pp | replace("+","") }}</td></tr>
  {%- endfor %}
  </tbody></table></div>
<p class="note" style="margin-bottom:34px">Spread is the gap between an assistant's best and worst market.
  A wide spread means the safeguards do not travel across languages equally.</p>

{%- if profiles.clusterGrid | length %}
<div class="shead"><h2>{{ 'section.clustersWhere' | t }}</h2></div>
<div class="panel"><table>
  <caption class="visually-hidden">Repeat-rate per narrative cluster in each market</caption>
  <thead><tr><th scope="col">{{ 'col.cluster' | t }}</th>
    {%- for c in profiles.countries %}<th scope="col">{{ c.key | flag }} {{ c.key | upper }}</th>{% endfor %}</tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {%- for row in profiles.clusterGrid %}
    <tr><td>{{ clusters[row.cluster].name_en | default(row.cluster) }}</td>
      {%- for c in profiles.countries %}
      <td class="rmeta">{% if row.cells[c.key] is defined %}{{ row.cells[c.key] | rate }}{% else %}<span style="color:var(--dimmer)">&mdash;</span>{% endif %}</td>
      {%- endfor %}</tr>
  {%- endfor %}
  </tbody></table></div>
<p class="note" style="margin-bottom:44px">A cluster that registers in one market and not another shows
  the operation localising its themes, not just its language.</p>
{%- endif %}
